From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:43:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: exynos: power the gs201 device down in system
 suspend

gs101_ufs_suspend(), which gs201 shares, drives HCI_GPIO_OUT low and so
asserts the device reset, and nothing releases it on resume. At the core's
default system PM level (3: device in SLEEP, link in Hibern8) the first
Hibern8 exit after resume therefore fails, and the error handler has to
reset the host and the device:

  ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit: hibern8 exit failed. ret = 5
  __ufshcd_wl_resume: ...
  ... Power mode changed to : FAST series_B G_4 L_2

That recovered without I/O errors on a Pixel 7 Pro (gs201) in a
suspend-to-idle dry run with pm_test=platform, but it turns every resume
into error recovery. With spm_lvl set to 5 at runtime (device powered
down, link off) the next real suspend-to-idle cycle resumed with no UFS
error, since resume from that level re-initialises the link and the
device anyway, which matches the reset.

Make level 5 the gs201 default, as Google's downstream driver does for
system suspend (exynos_ufs_override_hba_params()). Runtime PM keeps the
core default. gs101 probably wants the same, but is left alone here
because it hasn't been tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
index eb352f56e..15a2c9091 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -243,6 +243,21 @@ static int gs101_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
 	return exynos_ufs_shareability(ufs);
 }
 
+static int gs201_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
+{
+	/*
+	 * gs101_ufs_suspend() asserts the device reset, so the link can't
+	 * stay in Hibern8 across system suspend: at the default level the
+	 * first Hibern8 exit on resume fails and the error handler has to
+	 * reset the host and the device. Power the device down and turn the
+	 * link off instead, which resumes through a full re-init, as the
+	 * downstream driver does.
+	 */
+	ufs->hba->spm_lvl = UFS_PM_LVL_5;
+
+	return gs101_ufs_drv_init(ufs);
+}
+
 static int exynosauto_ufs_drv_init(struct exynos_ufs *ufs)
 {
 	return exynos_ufs_shareability(ufs);
@@ -2325,7 +2340,7 @@ static const struct exynos_ufs_drv_data gs201_ufs_drvs = {
 				  EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_UFSPR_SECURE |
 				  EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_TIMER_TICK_SELECT,
 	.iocc_mask		= UFS_GS101_SHARABLE,
-	.drv_init		= gs101_ufs_drv_init,
+	.drv_init		= gs201_ufs_drv_init,
 	.pre_link		= gs201_ufs_pre_link,
 	.post_link		= gs101_ufs_post_link,
 	.pre_pwr_change		= gs101_ufs_pre_pwr_change,
